","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:43:13Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T16:40:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6 stable, where the SSR is overhauled.\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 22.04.5 LTS 22.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900HX (32 threads) - 31.03 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe existing implementation of SSR has a subtle visual artifact: reflections on rough surfaces have inconsistent look at different distances. Specifically, they become more glossy as the camera moves away.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26dd8c2b-437c-4355-ad0a-8e9771031d09)\n\nI currently implemented [PR#115904](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115904) to address it. Technical reasoning about the issue and its math is provided there.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nObservable in any scene with non-zero roughness materials and SSR enabled. Please refer to MRP for details.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[ssr_enhancement_demo.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25096655/ssr_enhancement_demo.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{